{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-sonnet-5","packSha":"801c2da72d4ca39c5247ef222e8c4d97b03c0d0300d5cc62d529b9904b126bd4","packTokens":5044,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":54,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":4964,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The invoice reminders system shall classify an invoice as overdue, working this out on every request and never storing it, only when its status in the existing system is in the configured open-status list (default ['open']), it has a due date, and the number of calendar days from its due date to today's date, both taken in the configured business time zone, is at least the configured overdue threshold (default 7).\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given threshold is the default 7, business time zone Europe/London, the injected clock set to 2026-10-15, and open invoices due 2026-10-08 and 2026-10-09 when OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice then the call for the invoice due 2026-10-08 returns overdue = true and daysOverdue = 7, and the call for the invoice due 2026-10-09 returns overdue = false and daysOverdue = 6\",\n    \"Given threshold set to 10, today 2026-10-15, and open invoices due 2026-10-07, 2026-10-06 and 2026-10-05 when OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice then the calls return overdue = false for the invoices due 2026-10-07 and 2026-10-06, and overdue = true for the invoice due 2026-10-05\",\n    \"Given threshold 7, default open-status list ['open'], and seven invoices each 20 days past due with statuses paid, cancelled, draft, void, written-off, disputed and credited when OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for each invoice then every call returns overdue = false\",\n    \"Given threshold 7 and an invoice with status 'open' and a null due date when OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called for it then the call returns overdue = false and throws no exception\",\n    \"Given business time zone Europe/London, default threshold, and an open invoice due 2026-09-01 when OverduePolicy.Evaluate is called at instant 2026-09-07T22:30Z (23:30 on 7 Sep local), then at 2026-09-07T23:30Z (00:30 on 8 Sep local) then the first call returns daysOverdue = 6 and overdue = false, and the second returns daysOverdue = 7 and overdue = true\",\n    \"Given an open invoice due 6 days ago is not in the overdue list response, and no job or data change runs when the injected clock moves forward 1 day and the overdue list is requested again then the response now holds the invoice with daysOverdue = 7, and the invoice record in the existing database is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the Invoice Reminders API shall return every invoice currently classified as overdue, each with invoice ID, invoice number, customer name, amount, due date, days overdue (calendar days since the due date) and latest reminder outcome.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given today 2026-10-15, threshold 7, and in the existing database: open invoice A for customer 'Crumb & Co' with amount 125.50 due 2026-10-01, open invoice B due 2026-10-12, invoice C due 2026-09-01 with status paid, and invoice D due 2026-09-01 with status cancelled when an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list then the response is 200 and holds only invoice A, with its invoice number, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 125.50, due date 2026-10-01 and daysOverdue 14\",\n    \"Given invoice A is in the overdue list when its status in the existing system is changed to paid and the overdue list is requested again then invoice A is no longer in the response and no overdue flag was written to the invoice record\",\n    \"Given overdue invoice A with no reminder attempts and overdue invoice E whose latest attempt failed when the overdue list is requested then the response shows invoice A with latest reminder outcome null and invoice E with latest reminder outcome 'failed'\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only the overdue invoices that belong to that customer.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given customer X has 2 overdue invoices, customer Y has 1 overdue invoice, and customer Z has none when an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list with customerId = X, then with customerId = Z then the first response holds exactly customer X's 2 invoices and the second response is 200 with an empty list\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue fall inside the named fixed bucket (7–30, 31–60 or 61+, limits inclusive, not shifted by the configured overdue threshold), or respond 400 with a validation error when the bucket value is not one of these.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given default threshold 7 and overdue invoices at 7, 30, 31, 60, 61 and 90 days overdue when the overdue list is requested with bucket 7–30, then 31–60, then 61+ then the responses hold {7, 30}, {31, 60} and {61, 90}\",\n    \"Given customers X and Y each have overdue invoices at 10 and 45 days when the overdue list is requested with customerId = X and bucket 31–60, then with customerId = X and bucket 7–30 then the first response holds only X's 45-day invoice and the second holds only X's 10-day invoice\",\n    \"Given any overdue invoices when the overdue list is requested with an unknown bucket value such as '5-6' then the response is 400 with a validation error naming the bucket parameter\",\n    \"Given the overdue threshold is set to 5 and an open invoice is 6 days past due when the overdue list is requested without a bucket, then with bucket 7–30, 31–60 and 61+ then the invoice is in the unfiltered response and is in none of the three bucket responses\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests a reminder for an overdue invoice whose customer has a billing email, the Invoice Reminders API shall send one email through the configured email sender to that billing email, from the configured sender address, using the fixed template that contains the invoice number, the amount in local currency and the due date.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given overdue invoice INV-1042 with amount 245.50, due 2026-10-01, whose customer has billing email accounts@bakery.example, and a stub email sender that accepts messages when an authenticated staff user calls the send-reminder endpoint for INV-1042 then the response is 2xx with outcome 'sent', and the stub receives exactly one message addressed only to accounts@bakery.example, from the configured sender address, whose body contains 'INV-1042', '£245.50' and the due date in the configured date format\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a reminder is requested for an overdue invoice whose customer has no billing email, then the Invoice Reminders API shall send no email, reject the request with a 'missing billing email' error, and record the attempt in the reminder history as failed.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given an overdue invoice whose customer's billing email is null or empty, and a stub email sender when an authenticated staff user calls the send-reminder endpoint for it then the response is 422 with error code 'missing_billing_email' and a message saying the billing email is missing, the stub receives no message, and one reminder history row exists for the invoice with outcome 'failed' and reason 'missing billing email'\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a reminder is requested for an invoice that exists but is not overdue, including a paid or cancelled invoice, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject the request with a 409 error, send no email and add no reminder history entry.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given threshold 7, an open invoice INV-1050 that is 3 days past due, an invoice INV-1051 with status paid that is 40 days past due, and a stub email sender when an authenticated staff user calls the send-reminder endpoint for INV-1050, then for INV-1051 then both responses are 409 with an error saying the invoice is not overdue, the stub receives no message, and no reminder history row exists for either invoice\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a reminder send attempt for an overdue invoice finishes, the Invoice Reminders API shall add one row to the reminder history table in the Postgres database holding the invoice ID, the ID of the authenticated staff user who sent it, the server UTC timestamp of the attempt, the outcome (sent or failed) and the failure reason when there is one.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given staff user 'jane' is authenticated, overdue invoice INV-1 has no reminder history, and the stub email sender succeeds when jane sends a reminder for INV-1 at 2026-10-15T09:00:00Z then exactly one history row exists for INV-1 with jane's user ID as sender, timestamp 2026-10-15T09:00:00Z (±5 s), outcome 'sent' and no failure reason\",\n    \"Given INV-1 already has one 'sent' history row when staff user 'tom' sends another reminder for INV-1 then two rows exist for INV-1, the first row is unchanged, and the new row has tom's user ID as sender\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Invoice Reminders API shall answer every request to edit or delete a reminder history entry with HTTP 404 or 405 and leave the entry unchanged.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given an invoice with one reminder history entry with a known ID when an authenticated staff user sends PUT, PATCH and DELETE requests to the invoice's reminders collection path and to that entry's path then each response is 404 or 405 and the entry's row in the database is unchanged\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests an invoice's details, the Invoice Reminders API shall return the invoice number, customer name, amount, due date, overdue flag, days overdue, the latest reminder outcome taken from the newest history entry, and the full reminder history newest first, with each entry's sender, timestamp, outcome and failure reason.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given overdue invoice INV-1042 with attempts failed on 2026-10-10 by u-17 (reason 'SMTP 554'), then sent on 2026-10-12 by u-20 when an authenticated staff user requests INV-1042's details then the response holds amount, due date, overdue = true, latest outcome 'sent', and the history with the 2026-10-12 entry (u-20, sent) first and the 2026-10-10 entry (u-17, failed, 'SMTP 554') second\",\n    \"Given an overdue invoice with no reminder history when its details are requested then the response has an empty history list and latest outcome null\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If the email sender returns an error when a reminder is handed to it, then the Invoice Reminders API shall return an error response with outcome 'failed' and the error reason, record the attempt as failed with the sender's error message as the reason, and keep the invoice in the overdue list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given overdue invoice INV-1042 with a billing email, and a stub email sender set to throw 'SMTP 554 rejected' when an authenticated staff user calls the send-reminder endpoint then the response is 502 and reports outcome 'failed' with a reason containing 'SMTP 554 rejected', and a history row with outcome 'failed' and that reason is stored\",\n    \"Given the failed attempt in AC-13.1 has happened when the overdue list and the invoice details are requested then INV-1042 is still in the overdue list response with latest reminder outcome 'failed', and the details response shows latest outcome 'failed' with reason containing 'SMTP 554 rejected'\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint has no valid staff authentication from the existing API, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 without returning invoice data, sending email or changing data.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given no token, and separately an expired token when the overdue list, invoice detail and send-reminder endpoints are called then each response is 401 with no invoice or customer data in the body, the stub email sender receives no message, and no history row is added\",\n    \"Given a valid token for any staff user with no special role when the overdue list, invoice detail and send-reminder endpoints are called for an overdue invoice with a billing email then none returns 401 or 403 and each succeeds (2xx)\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If an invoice detail or send-reminder request names an invoice ID that does not exist in the existing system, then the Invoice Reminders API shall respond with HTTP 404, send no email and add no reminder history row.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given no invoice with ID 999999 exists in the existing database when an authenticated staff user requests GET /api/invoices/999999 then the response is 404 and its body holds no invoice or customer data\",\n    \"Given no invoice with ID 999999 exists and a stub email sender is configured when an authenticated staff user calls POST /api/invoices/999999/reminders then the response is 404, the stub receives no message, and no reminder history row with invoice ID 999999 exists\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"The overdue list endpoint meets the stated latency at the stated data volumes, with or without filters.\",\n  \"The send-reminder endpoint waits a limited time for the email sender and records a timeout as a failed attempt.\",\n  \"Customer PII (billing email addresses), invoice amounts and reminder email bodies are kept out of application logs.\",\n  \"All Invoice Reminders endpoints require authentication.\",\n  \"Reminder history is durable and append-only: the application never removes or changes history rows.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}